  "RightSideDisplay": 10,
  "RightSideHtmlBlock": "<h4>Risk reporting matrix</h4><p>Rate the likelihood and the cost, schedule and performance consequence of this move's risk as if fully realized. The consequence is the <b>greatest</b> of the three (e.g. cost 2, schedule 3, performance 2 is a 3). Read the risk level from the matrix. Only the risk level is scored.</p><p>Rows: likelihood; columns: consequence 1 to 5.</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"6\" cellspacing=\"0\"><tr><th></th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td><td>High</td><td>High</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td><td>Moderate</td><td>High</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td><td>Moderate</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Low</td><td>Moderate</td></tr></table><p>A probability of 1 (or approaching 1) is an issue, not a risk.</p><p><i>Source: Department of Defense Risk, Issue, and Opportunity (RIO) Management Guide for Defense Acquisition Programs (OUSD(R&amp;E), September 2023), Tables 2-1 and 2-2 and Figure 2-5. Distribution Statement A. The guide's levels are ordinal; it advises against fractional scores. Figure 2-5 is shown with likelihood 5 at the top, as in the guide's Figure 2-6.</i></p>",
